WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.815 --> 00:00:08.215
♫ One two ♫

00:00:08.215 --> 00:00:10.255
- I feel like there's like a glass ceiling

00:00:10.255 --> 00:00:12.838
for women, because I've hit it.

00:00:14.422 --> 00:00:15.798
If you skate and you rip

00:00:15.798 --> 00:00:17.547
then you should just get what you deserve,

00:00:17.547 --> 00:00:22.443
if like skateboarding is
supposed to be for everybody.

00:00:22.443 --> 00:00:25.557
If we do actually want any
form of equality or space,

00:00:25.557 --> 00:00:29.724
like, we're gonna have to be
the ones who create that space.

00:00:33.078 --> 00:00:35.833
(electronic music)

00:00:35.833 --> 00:00:39.696
My name is Lacey Baker and I'm
a professional skateboarder.

00:00:39.696 --> 00:00:41.858
I discovered skateboarding
when I was really really young,

00:00:41.858 --> 00:00:43.314
at like two years old.

00:00:43.314 --> 00:00:44.659
I was in foster care at that time

00:00:44.659 --> 00:00:46.529
and I would watch my foster brothers skate

00:00:46.529 --> 00:00:50.065
a mini ramp, and I just
was like immediately obsessed.

00:00:50.065 --> 00:00:53.309
Like I was like I have to do this.

00:00:53.309 --> 00:00:55.343
I started competing
when I was 11 years old.

00:00:55.343 --> 00:00:58.652
When I was 22, I skated
the 2014 X Games in Austin

00:00:58.652 --> 00:01:01.569
and that's the year I won the gold.

00:01:06.137 --> 00:01:07.157
With women in skateboarding,

00:01:07.157 --> 00:01:09.807
there's like a subculture
within a subculture.

00:01:09.807 --> 00:01:12.430
The skate industry like just doesn't care

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:14.254
about women skating.

00:01:14.254 --> 00:01:15.135
It's not equal.

00:01:15.135 --> 00:01:18.046
For example, like, there is
this skateboard contest series

00:01:18.046 --> 00:01:20.903
which didn't used to include women in it

00:01:20.903 --> 00:01:23.321
but it just started to.

00:01:23.321 --> 00:01:25.916
However, the prize for
first place is 30 grand,

00:01:25.916 --> 00:01:29.479
and like for the guys
first place is 200 grand.

00:01:29.479 --> 00:01:31.166
I feel like it should
be equal because we work

00:01:31.166 --> 00:01:33.249
just as hard as the guys.

00:01:34.413 --> 00:01:36.360
Meow Skateboards is a
company that was created

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.868
to, like, support women in skateboarding.

00:01:38.868 --> 00:01:40.827
I do my own board graphics,
like I do a lot of

00:01:40.827 --> 00:01:42.296
the other girls' board graphics.

00:01:42.296 --> 00:01:44.888
And like, it's rad because
it's, like, skater owned,

00:01:44.888 --> 00:01:46.816
and it's, like, for us,
and it's, like, by us.

00:01:46.816 --> 00:01:49.761
So it's like, there's
nothing corporate about it.

00:01:49.761 --> 00:01:53.844
And it feels like that's
how it's supposed to be.

00:01:54.705 --> 00:01:58.368
Even if nothing comes of,
like, having a skate career

00:01:58.368 --> 00:02:02.009
or like, anything like that,
like, I still have skating.

00:02:02.009 --> 00:02:03.730
And, like, I believe in being yourself,

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:06.238
and, like, just doing
whatever the fuck you want,

00:02:06.238 --> 00:02:09.405
and that's what skating is supposed to be.

